                                "sense_id": "c483b719-f335-3118-9b8f-3516d7adf2c8",
                                "text": "Commonly called aeolids, these nudibranchs have cerata (usually in groups) along each side of the body, each ceras containing a duct of the digestive gland and usually having a cavity (cnidosac) to store ingested nematocysts in the tip, which distinguishes aeolids from all other nudibranchs."
